jobs.description:
As a Financial Controller, you will have a broad range of responsibilities, including:


• Analyzing financial results and discussing them with regional management;

• Optimizing processes related to ongoing operations and gross margin performance;

• Developing initiatives aimed at improving profitability;

• Ensuring an up-to-date SAP structure and delivering accurate financial forecasts;

• Preparing budgets using SAP BPC tools;

• Representing the organization during local management meetings;

• Ensuring compliance with financial processes and supporting audit activities;

• Supporting cost control initiatives and handling ad-hoc financial tasks.

Your profile:


• You hold a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a financial or related field;

• You have at least initial experience in finance, for example as a consultant or Financial Controller;

• Experience with audits is a plus;

• A strong knowledge of Excel is essential; experience with SAP is an advantage;

• You have excellent written and verbal communication skills in English (knowledge of other languages is a plus);

• You are a team player, work accurately, and are able to meet deadlines;

• You take a proactive, problem solving approach and feel comfortable in a dynamic environment.
